{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/966019-we-are-all-cyborgs","id":966019,"title":"We Are All Cyborgs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-08T20:45:46-07:00","id":966019,"title":"We Are All Cyborgs","content":"Everyone reading this is a transhumanist. Everyone on this forum is a transhumanist. Most people have never met anyone who wasn't a transhumanist. Almost every work of fiction ever is pro-transhumanism. <br /> <br /> Why? Because each and every one of us is a cyborg. A cyborg is any entity that uses technology to expand its capabilities beyond natural limits or compensate for things it has lost or does not have. <br /> <br /> I am a cyborg. <br /> <br /> I am a cyborg because I drive a car. When I combine myself with this machine by entering it, I can move much faster and much more easily than I can without it. <br /> <br /> I am a cyborg because I take medicine and do physical therapy exercises. I apply scientific knowledge by means of synthesized chemicals and exercises and use it to alter the functions of my body. <br /> <br /> I am a cyborg because I wear clothes. I cover my skin with an artificial skin for reasons of comfort, hygiene, and aesthetics. <br /> <br /> Each and every one of you is a cyborg, because if you are reading this you are using a computer, a device that allows you to do things far beyond natural human capabilities. Every Onyx Path writer is a cyborg transhumanist, as is every other writer and artist in history, because to write or make art you must become a cyborg. <br /> <br /> Humans have been cyborgs since the first hominid picked up a rock. Rocks, sticks, writing, fire, and agriculture all make us cyborgs. We are all transhumanists because we all believe that it is good to use technology to surpass human limits. If you think airplanes are a good invention, you are a transhumanist. If you think pens are a good invention, you are a transhumanist. If you see doctors and get vaccinations and take medicine, you are a transhumanist, because you believe in using technology to repair your body and extend its lifespan beyond natural limits. <br /> <br /> Humans are natural cyborgs. <br /> <br /> Think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:01:39-07:00","id":966024,"title":"","content":"I may be a cyborg, but I won't be a <i>happy</i> cyborg until I get cyber eyes that can shoot laser beams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:03:13-07:00","id":966025,"title":"","content":"Oh, definitely same. It's just something to think about for those who think &quot;natural&quot; is a meaningful descriptor and/or a desirable quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:15:08-07:00","id":966054,"title":"","content":"As someone with poor eyes, a warped spine, a fragile heart, a terrible digestive system, and body dysphoria... yeah, this isn't the stripe of cyborg I want. Not yet. Wake me up when I can go full digital consciousness transhuman immortality and enjoy my proper, beautiful, synthetic body on the slope of Olympus Mons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:41:12-07:00","id":966085,"title":"","content":"Webster disagrees<br /> <br /> cy\u00b7borg<br /> \u02c8s\u012b\u02ccb\u00f4r\u0261/<br /> noun<br /> a fictional or hypothetical person whose physical abilities are extended beyond normal human limitations by mechanical elements built into the body.<br /> <br /> So unless you have that cell phone built into your head I'm afraid you are not a cyborg.<br /> <br /> Also don't push your &quot;transhumanist&quot; agenda on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 09-09-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T01:34:45-07:00","id":966114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/966019-we-are-all-cyborgs#post966019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about it and... oh wait, it's bullshit. It's a disservice to transhumanism to dilute the definition by making it so broad it is meaningless. It's a disservice to basic human communication to claim a word means something it doesn't actually mean for the sole purpose of creating a fallacious semantic argument.<br /> <br /> I've always found the saddest form of advocacy for a specific philosophic stance to be attempts to claim, &quot;You aren't what you think you are, you're really one of my side all along!&quot; because it betrays a complete lack of confidence in the advocate's philosophy's ability to withstand actual rational analysis. If you really believe in transhumanism, you'd be able to advocate for it based on it's merits; not with word games that try to con people into thinking you're pointing out a cognitive dissonance when you're really just making a bad argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T09:42:12-07:00","id":966283,"title":"","content":"You do realize that I didn't come up with this idea, right? Look up Donna Haraway. The idea that humans are natural cyborgs is something that's been seriously debated and considered. It's not a &quot;word game&quot;. If you have a problem with the definition of cyborg that I'm using, you would have to take it up with Haraway, Andy Clark, or any of the other scientists and philosophers who have proposed that definition.<br /> <br /> And the point I was trying to make is that transhumanism isn't really an ideology. It's a guiding principle of human existence that each person happens to have a different threshold for.<br /> <br /> And if you insist on hewing to the dictionary definition...we already have artificial organs and prosthetic limbs. Do you think people who need these devices should be able to use them? Do you think that having a prosthetic doesn't make you less human? Then you're pro-cyborg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-09-2016, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:55:53-07:00","id":966334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/966019-we-are-all-cyborgs?p=966283#post966283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize that I didn't come up with this idea, right? Look up Donna Haraway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You.... realize that Haraway was using cyborgs as a metaphor, not actually claiming that humans are inherently cyborgs, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not a &quot;word game&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Yes it is. Just because other people do it to doesn't make it not a word game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have a problem with the definition of cyborg that I'm using, you would have to take it up with Haraway, Andy Clark, or any of the other scientists and philosophers who have proposed that definition. </div> </div> </div>No, I don't have to take it up with them. They're not coming to a space I choose to participate and insisting this definition should be given weight. You are. Appeals to authority are... oh wait just another form of fallacy. Various people &quot;seriously&quot; discussing a concept doesn't mean they're right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the point I was trying to make is that transhumanism isn't really an ideology. </div> </div> </div>No it isn't inherently an ideology (though lots of forms of transhumanism take base transhumanism and turn it into an ideology). It's still just a philosophic construct though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a guiding principle of human existence that each person happens to have a different threshold for. </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. What you're describing isn't &quot;transhumanism,&quot; its just humanism, because it has nothing to do with becoming posthuman. Humans have always been creative tool-users. Continuing to be so in more advanced ways does not change humans into posthumans, and thus is not transhumanism.<br /> <br /> As well, the idea of an &quot;inherent&quot; guiding principle essential to humanity is irrational from a scientific perspective. It's the same poor argumentation that results in people that think evolution has an &quot;end goal,&quot; instead of just being a continuous process with results constantly subject to the specifics of a situation with no destination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think people who need these devices should be able to use them? </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think that having a prosthetic doesn't make you less human? </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you're pro-cyborg. </div> </div> </div>Inappropriate conclusion.<br /> <br /> It means I'm not anti-cyborg. However, I don't believe that seeing the potential good in any given technology means having to be unquestionably pro that technology. Scientific and technological ethics requires nuance, not black and white &quot;you are either for or against things!&quot; nonsense.<br /> <br /> Also, being &quot;pro-cyborg&quot; doesn't actually mean I'm a transhumanist. I don't believe cybernetic augmentation of the human body constitutes a fundamental change of the human body into something different, so to me a cyborg isn't inherently a transitional state to posthumanity, it's just a human with modifications more technically advanced but not more philosophically important than a tattoo.<br /> <br /> Transhumanists don't actually have a lock on believing in improving the human condition through technology. It's one of the more insipid things to come out of the transhumanist echo-chamber: that if you believe in medical technology you belief in changing humans into posthumans; forgetting that tranhumanism is more than just technology impacting the human body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:41:03-07:00","id":966442,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely clear on the purpose of the exercise. Even if we all fall under your arbitrarily bounded definition of &quot;transhumanist&quot; what is it you're wanting us to get out of that? If you have a specific take away in mind just state it flatly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:13:10-07:00","id":966458,"title":"","content":"Cyborg is a contraction of cybernetic organism. Your premise is false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T17:44:24-07:00","id":966499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/966019-we-are-all-cyborgs?p=966442#post966442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely clear on the purpose of the exercise. Even if we all fall under your arbitrarily bounded definition of &quot;transhumanist&quot; what is it you're wanting us to get out of that? If you have a specific take away in mind just state it flatly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think gecko is rying ot prove that we shouldn't reject certain behaviors just because they may seem to make us inhuman or unnatural. since &quot;human&quot; and &quot;natural&quot; are quite subjective","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:11:21-07:00","id":966508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/966019-we-are-all-cyborgs?p=966499#post966499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think gecko is rying ot prove that we shouldn't reject certain behaviors just because they may seem to make us inhuman or unnatural. since &amp;quot;human&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;natural&amp;quot; are quite subjective</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this topic was spawned by a bunch of backlash against pursuing a transhumanist perspective in various on-topic threads. I'm not sure why, maybe to point out some sort of perceived hypocrisy? Regardless, like others in this thread I feel like the argument in the OP is based on misguided definitions of &quot;cyborg&quot; and &quot;transhumanism&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T21:05:00-07:00","id":966577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/966019-we-are-all-cyborgs?p=966499#post966499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think gecko is rying ot prove that we shouldn't reject certain behaviors just because they may seem to make us inhuman or unnatural. since &quot;human&quot; and &quot;natural&quot; are quite subjective</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem though, is that the argument is backwards.<br /> <br /> It's trying to say that &quot;natural&quot; shouldn't be treated as good, but the case is actually that technology <b>is natural</b>.<br /> <br /> Humans evolved as creative tool using technology making primates. Making tools, and improving on those tools, which improves our lives in return, is natural human behavior. Making new technologies is what we do as a species. It isn't an unnatural process as the word artificial has come to imply (instead of just meaning man-made in a more neutral fashion).<br /> <br /> You can't vilify &quot;natural&quot; to make &quot;technological&quot; look good with a sound argument. You can make technological look good by making a sound case that it is a subset of natural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:07:16-07:00","id":968873,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> Are you going to come back and tell us how wrong we all are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:23:30-07:00","id":969852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/966019-we-are-all-cyborgs#post966019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone reading this is a transhumanist. Everyone on this forum is a transhumanist. Most people have never met anyone who wasn't a transhumanist. Almost every work of fiction ever is pro-transhumanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transhumanism is downloading your consciousness onto machines to gain immortality and move beyond the material needs of living.<br /> <br /> I'm about as much a Transhumanist as I am Republican.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:41:28-07:00","id":969864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/966019-we-are-all-cyborgs?p=969852#post969852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transhumanism is downloading your consciousness onto machines to gain immortality and move beyond the material needs of living.<br /> <br /> I'm about as much a Transhumanist as I am Republican.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Transhumanism is more than that and less than what the OP said. It's about freely incorporating technological developments into your idea of what is human. Radical body modification is embraced, which includes downloading your consciousness onto a machine, but doesn't necessitate it. Wearing glasses or contacts is not transhumanist, nor is surgery to repair or even enhance vision, but getting a nose piercing that lets you bolt your lenses onto your face is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:05:31-07:00","id":970088,"title":"","content":"Actually, no to both.<br /> <br /> Transhumanism is the philosophic position that humans can actively shape themselves (during which they become tranhumans during their state of flux) into a superior state of being (aka posthuman).<br /> <br /> 1) Not all tranhumanist philosophies are secular or technological. Spiritual transhumanism is actually a thing, and it focuses on transforming in a more ephemeral way (focusing on concepts such as the mind, soul, spirit, etc), to transcend the limitations of the human body (including the brain).<br /> <br /> 2) Coherent tranhumanist philosophies include changes beyond alterations to the base human form. Body mods and cybernetics are not inherently transhumanist. Transhumanism requires psychological change that trickles into social, political, and economic social changes as well.<br /> <br /> 3) Any given form of transhumanism most define the posthuman in a fashion that demonstrates meaningful and complete change from base human. Any possible transhuman states have to be analyzed in the context of how the posthuman is defined. Simply modifying yourself in a fashion that doesn't have significant impact towards what you consider to be posthuman does not make you a transhuman. While I'm hesitant to make this comparison do to a significant semantic difference in how the prefix trans- is being applied, I think it is sufficiently illustrative of the point: A man that puts on female gendered clothing is not a transwoman. An AMAB individual transwoman might choose to wear female gendered clothing to affirm their status as transitioning from their assigned gender to their actual gender. You don't get a body mod and become transhuman. You choose to adopt a transhuman philosophy and getting a body mod (if compatible with that form of transhumanism) is part of starting towards the end goal of posthumanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:12:16-07:00","id":970093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/966019-we-are-all-cyborgs?p=966085#post966085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So unless you have that cell phone built into your head I'm afraid you are not a cyborg.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can I play Angry Birds, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 09-15-2016, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}